    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "One of the Catalinas which operate from Port Moresby to West\nPapua, to East Papua and to adjacent islands to the north-east.\nA Qantas Douglas airliner at a New Guinea airport. Qantas operates\ntwelve regular services and many charter services in the \"Territory\"\nNEW GUINEA \"BIRD OF PARADISE\" SERVICE\nINTERNAL SERVICES AND ISLANDS SERVICES\nLAKE MURRAY\nWEW AK\nWABAG\nBAIYER RIVER\nMT. HAGEN\nKEROW AGI\nMADANG\nNONDUG'-\nGOROKA\nKAINANTU\nAIYURA\nLAE\nLAKE KUT\nBULOLO\nDARU\nI KIKORI:\nWAU\nEMA\nKEREMA.\nYULE\nMORESBY\nMANUS ISLAND\nFINSCH HAFEN\n(AVIENG\nRABAUL\nTALASEA\nMOEWE\nCAROLA\nHBR\nBUKA PASSAGE\nSINUS\nJAQUINOT BAY\nKOKODA\nHIGATURA L\nABAU\nTOROKINA\nLOSUlA\nBUIN\n- ESA ALA\nVELLA LAVELL\nSAMARA\nDEBOYNE IS\nPacific\nOcean:\nTimo\nYANDINAY\nCAIRNS\nCoral Se\nHONIAR\nTOWNSVILLE\nAUSTRALIA\nROCKHAMPTON\nSUVA\n- VILA\nBRISBANE\nESPIRITU SANTO\nNOUMEA\nLEGEND\nLEYDNEY\nREGULAR SERVICES\n1 FREQUENT NON-SCHEDULED FLIGHTS\nNORFOLK ISLAND",
      "The Kava Ceremony, Fiji.\nQANTAS EMPIRE AIRWAYS\nBooking offices at: SYDNEY, MELBOURNE, BRISBANE, PORT\nMORESBY, LAE, DARWIN, SINGAPORE. And leading travel\nagents everywhere.\nCascades, Norfolk Island.",
      "BIRD OF PARADISE\nSERVICE\nQANTAS EMPIRE AIRWAYS"
    ],
